    "updated_at": "2026-11-08T20:48:09Z",
    "body": "**For maintainer review: the consensus threshold.**\n\nThis fallback accepts an axis when **75 %** of the answering surface meets the consensus line (`CONSENSUS_SHARE` in `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/axis_consensus.rs`). The plain gate needs 90 %, and the robust pass's backstop is 50 %. The contributor isn't positioned to judge the right number, so this needs your call. Two things limit the risk:\n\n- The fallback runs only when no candidate passes the plain 90 % gate. Every part that fitted before gets exactly the same fit, and no golden changed.\n- The off-axis-lump (30 % of the surface) and box cases are still refused by name (pinned in `axis_consensus_tests` and `lathe_spindle_keyed`).\n\nIf you want a different share, it is one constant; the tests pin both sides of it. Flagging the PR ready so it reaches your queue. The rest is in `docs/decisions/113-lathe-axis-fit.md`.\n",
